# candor-swift self-gate (SPEC §7.12): the analyzer reads source and writes reports — Fs/Env are its
# job. It must never reach the network, a database, or local IPC.
#
# It spawns a subprocess in exactly TWO places, both in main.swift, and both are "run a tool again":
# the `--workspace` chain spawns candor-swift itself on each workspace dependency and reads the report
# back through a Pipe (Exec + Ipc), and the Xcode-scope resolution shells out via `/usr/bin/env` to
# resolve a target. Those are the feature, not a hidden effect.
#
# A prefix deny cannot say "deny Exec everywhere except main.swift", so CI proves the two halves
# separately (candor-java and candor-ts split the same problem the same way — see
# .github/workflows/ci.yml):
#   (1) the analysis CORE (main.swift removed) under THIS policy — no Exec/Ipc either;
#   (2) the WHOLE engine under `deny Net Db` — still no network, still no database.
# Together: candor-swift reaches the network or a database nowhere, and spawns a process only in the
# one file that says it does.
#
# This file is the declared boundary and CI reads it. It used to be a `printf` inside the workflow,
# which meant the repository declared no policy at all: `candor-swift .` here applied nothing, and the
# boundary existed only in a CI step nobody reads.
deny Net Db Exec Ipc
